## 3. R2 exact corrections

### 3.1 Replacement-object closure

Every future Git invocation executed by the R2 runner uses an empty inherited
environment whose closed Git portion includes:

    GIT_NO_REPLACE_OBJECTS=1
    GIT_ALTERNATE_OBJECT_DIRECTORIES=
    GIT_DIR=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git
    GIT_OBJECT_DIRECTORY=/home/jenn/AGENTS_OS_Workspace/runtime/VCPToolBox/.git/objects
    GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1
    GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null

The runner rejects a missing or substituted value in its synthetic fixture.
The R2 validator includes a replacement-object mutation. No future source run
may rely on a default Git replacement policy.

### 3.2 Executable subject closure

The runner and scanner are new R2 subjects:

    runner: control-plane/registry/run-phase-5d-m0d-actual-object-only-source-run-r2.py
    scanner: control-plane/registry/object-only-source-run-r2-scanner.py

The runner accepts no caller-selected root, ref, object ID, tuple, output path,
or cleanup target. It has only synthetic fixture/self-test modes by default.
Its actual mode is inert unless a later Jenn decision separately names its
hash-bound bytes and explicitly selects that mode.

The scanner consumes only a NUL-delimited name-only tree stream. It neither
invokes Git nor reads a blob. It compares the protected subset against the
frozen seven-name inventory without printing a name or object identifier.

### 3.3 Path, receipt, temporary-result, and finalizer closure

The runner must:

1. use lstat and exact realpath equality to reject a canonical-root symlink;
2. reject a symlink Git directory, object directory, object-info directory,
   alternates file, run root, or receipt target;
3. create the run root with mkdir mode 0700, then create the ownership marker,
   then create the temporary result, each by O_CREAT, O_EXCL, and O_NOFOLLOW;
4. create the final receipt only after finalization, also by O_CREAT, O_EXCL,
   and O_NOFOLLOW;
5. block SIGINT, SIGTERM, and SIGHUP before installing their handlers, restore
   the prior mask only after the handlers are installed, block them again for
   cleanup and receipt finalization, and run the owned-root finalizer in all
   catchable interruption paths; and
6. treat SIGKILL, process crash, missing marker, missing temporary result,
   residue, receipt collision, no-follow failure, or finalizer failure as a
   non-success outcome.

The finalizer is restricted to the two literal newly created files and the
literal run root. It uses no recursive deletion, glob, worktree command, or
Host cleanup method.

